**Basic REST controller**
- Same annotations as MVC; return `Mono<T>` / `Flux<T>`
- `switchIfEmpty` is the idiomatic 404
- `@Valid` on a `@RequestBody Mono<T>` triggers reactive validation

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/orders")
public class OrderController {

    private final OrderService service;

    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public Mono<OrderDto> get(@PathVariable String id) {
        return service.load(id)
            .switchIfEmpty(Mono.error(new OrderNotFound(id)));
    }

    @GetMapping
    public Flux<OrderDto> list(
            @RequestParam(defaultValue = "20") int size,
            @RequestParam(required = false) String status) {
        return service.search(status).take(size);
    }

    @PostMapping
    @ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.CREATED)
    public Mono<OrderDto> create(@Valid @RequestBody Mono<CreateOrder> body) {
        return body.flatMap(service::create);
    }

    @GetMapping(value = "/events", produces = MediaType.TEXT_EVENT_STREAM_VALUE)
    public Flux<ServerSentEvent<OrderEvent>> stream() {
        return service.eventStream()
            .map(e -> ServerSentEvent.builder(e)
                .id(e.id())
                .event(e.type())
                .build());
    }
}
```

**Notes**
- `Mono<RequestBody>` lets you process the body as a reactive stream; plain `@RequestBody Foo` materializes it
- SSE — return `Flux<ServerSentEvent<T>>` with `produces = MediaType.TEXT_EVENT_STREAM_VALUE`
- Validation errors propagate as `WebExchangeBindException`
- Content negotiation via `produces` and `consumes` works as in MVC
- Use `ResponseEntity<Mono<T>>` only when you need custom headers or status; direct `Mono<T>` is usually cleaner

**RouterFunction configuration**
- Routes declared in one place
- Composable filters via `.filter(...)`

```java
@Configuration
public class OrderRouter {

    @Bean
    public RouterFunction<ServerResponse> routes(OrderHandler h) {
        return route(GET("/orders/{id}"), h::get)
            .andRoute(GET("/orders"), h::list)
            .andRoute(POST("/orders"), h::create)
            .andRoute(GET("/orders/events").and(accept(TEXT_EVENT_STREAM)), h::stream)
            .filter((req, next) -> {
                log.debug("request: {}", req.path());
                return next.handle(req);
            });
    }
}
```

**Handler component**
- Methods take `ServerRequest`, return `Mono<ServerResponse>`
- Body access via `req.bodyToMono(Type.class)`

```java
@Component
public class OrderHandler {

    private final OrderService service;

    public Mono<ServerResponse> get(ServerRequest req) {
        String id = req.pathVariable("id");
        return service.load(id)
            .flatMap(order -> ServerResponse.ok()
                .contentType(APPLICATION_JSON).bodyValue(order))
            .switchIfEmpty(ServerResponse.notFound().build());
    }

    public Mono<ServerResponse> create(ServerRequest req) {
        return req.bodyToMono(CreateOrder.class)
            .flatMap(service::create)
            .flatMap(created -> ServerResponse
                .created(URI.create("/orders/" + created.id()))
                .bodyValue(created));
    }

    public Mono<ServerResponse> stream(ServerRequest req) {
        return ServerResponse.ok()
            .contentType(TEXT_EVENT_STREAM)
            .body(service.eventStream(), OrderEvent.class);
    }
}
```

**When functional wins**
- Routes declared in one place
- API gateway or small service
- You prefer explicit request / response over annotations
- You need conditional / composable route predicates

**When annotated wins**
- Team already fluent in MVC annotations
- Onboarding cost matters
- Lots of OpenAPI / Swagger annotations
- Mixed services where consistency with MVC modules matters

Both styles can coexist in one application.

**One bean per upstream — never share a `WebClient` across upstreams with different configs.**

```java
@Configuration
public class WebClients {

    @Bean("paymentsClient")
    public WebClient paymentsClient(WebClient.Builder builder) {
        HttpClient http = HttpClient.create(ConnectionProvider.builder("pay")
                .maxConnections(200)
                .pendingAcquireTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
                .build())
            .responseTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(3))
            .option(ChannelOption.CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MILLIS, 2000)
            .doOnConnected(conn -> conn
                .addHandlerLast(new ReadTimeoutHandler(5))
                .addHandlerLast(new WriteTimeoutHandler(5)));

        return builder
            .baseUrl("https://payments.internal")
            .clientConnector(new ReactorClientHttpConnector(http))
            .defaultHeader(HttpHeaders.USER_AGENT, "orders/1.0")
            .filter(logRequest())
            .filter(authHeader())
            .build();
    }

    private ExchangeFilterFunction logRequest() {
        return ExchangeFilterFunction.ofRequestProcessor(req -> {
            log.debug("{} {}", req.method(), req.url());
            return Mono.just(req);
        });
    }
}
```

**Using it**
- `.onStatus` for explicit 4xx / 5xx mapping
- `.timeout` per call for tighter control
- `.retryWhen(Retry.backoff(...))` filtered to retryable errors

```java
@Service
public class PaymentClient {
    private final WebClient client;

    public Mono<PaymentResult> charge(Charge req) {
        return client.post().uri("/charge")
            .contentType(APPLICATION_JSON)
            .bodyValue(req)
            .retrieve()
            .onStatus(HttpStatusCode::is4xxClientError,
                r -> r.bodyToMono(String.class)
                    .flatMap(body -> Mono.error(new ClientError(body))))
            .onStatus(HttpStatusCode::is5xxServerError,
                r -> Mono.error(new UpstreamError()))
            .bodyToMono(PaymentResult.class)
            .timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
            .retryWhen(Retry.backoff(3, Duration.ofMillis(200))
                .filter(e -> e instanceof UpstreamError));
    }
}
```

**Production essentials**
- Connection pool tuned (`maxConnections`, `pendingAcquireTimeout`)
- Response timeout plus `ReadTimeoutHandler` and `WriteTimeoutHandler`
- Connect timeout
- 4xx / 5xx handling via `onStatus`
- Retry with backoff and jitter, filtered to retryable exceptions
- Circuit breaker via Resilience4j
- Logging / metrics filters
- mTLS / TLS via `SslContextBuilder` if needed

**`WebFilter` for cross-cutting concerns**
- Implements `WebFilter` and `filter(exchange, chain)`
- Use `Context.of` to propagate values like trace ID into the reactive chain
- `@Order` controls execution order

```java
@Component
public class TracingFilter implements WebFilter {
    @Override
    public Mono<Void> filter(ServerWebExchange exchange, WebFilterChain chain) {
        String traceId = Optional.ofNullable(exchange.getRequest().getHeaders()
                .getFirst("X-Trace-Id"))
            .orElseGet(() -> UUID.randomUUID().toString());
        exchange.getResponse().getHeaders().add("X-Trace-Id", traceId);
        return chain.filter(exchange)
            .contextWrite(Context.of("traceId", traceId));
    }
}
```

**Reactive security**

```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebFluxSecurity
class SecurityConfig {
    @Bean
    SecurityWebFilterChain chain(ServerHttpSecurity http) {
        return http
            .csrf(ServerHttpSecurity.CsrfSpec::disable)
            .authorizeExchange(ex -> ex
                .pathMatchers("/actuator/health").permitAll()
                .pathMatchers(HttpMethod.GET, "/orders/**").authenticated()
                .anyExchange().authenticated())
            .oauth2ResourceServer(o -> o.jwt(Customizer.withDefaults()))
            .build();
    }
}
```

**CORS — `CorsWebFilter`, not `CorsFilter`**

```java
@Bean
CorsWebFilter corsFilter() {
    CorsConfiguration cfg = new CorsConfiguration();
    cfg.setAllowedOrigins(List.of("https://app.example.com"));
    cfg.setAllowedMethods(List.of("GET", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE"));
    cfg.setAllowedHeaders(List.of("*"));
    cfg.setAllowCredentials(true);
    UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource src = new UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource();
    src.registerCorsConfiguration("/**", cfg);
    return new CorsWebFilter(src);
}
```

**Testing with `WebTestClient` and `StepVerifier`**

```java
@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = RANDOM_PORT)
class OrderIT {
    @Autowired WebTestClient client;

    @Test
    void getOrder() {
        client.get().uri("/orders/abc")
            .exchange()
            .expectStatus().isOk()
            .expectBody(OrderDto.class)
            .value(o -> assertThat(o.id()).isEqualTo("abc"));
    }

    @Test
    void streamEvents() {
        client.get().uri("/orders/events")
            .accept(TEXT_EVENT_STREAM)
            .exchange()
            .expectStatus().isOk()
            .returnResult(new ParameterizedTypeReference<ServerSentEvent<OrderEvent>>() {})
            .getResponseBody()
            .take(3)
            .as(StepVerifier::create)
            .expectNextCount(3)
            .thenCancel()
            .verify(Duration.ofSeconds(5));
    }
}
```
